  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_045 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clear outlier at 0.706 acc, far exceeding the singleprofile multimodal configs (~0.53–0.54). The dominant driver is the multiprofile setting with aggregation. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the simple avgpool aggregation is near-optimal or whether a more expressive transformer aggregation could capture inter-profile interactions and push performance higher. This experiment (config_043) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other parameters identical to config_045 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile). It cleanly isolates the aggregation effect in the multiprofile regime. Under a limited budget, this is the best next step because it directly tests the most impactful potential improvement to our current best configuration; a positive result would justify further aggregation exploration, while a null result would confirm avgpool sufficiency and redirect effort toward encoder or fusion choices."
}

